From: Peter Strand <peter@zarquon.se>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arm64: dts: apple: t8112: add sep alias and enable the node

The SEP node is declared but disabled, and there is no "sep" alias, so
m1n1's dt_set_sep() returns early at

    const char *path = fdt_get_alias(dt, "sep");
    if (path == NULL) { ... return 0; }

and never reserves the sepfw region or attaches the local-policy-manifest /
iboot-manifest properties that the driver's probe() requires. dt_set_sep()
also does not touch status, so that has to be flipped here.

This is a "turn it on so we can look at it" patch, not something to merge:
booting SEPOS on a machine whose driver is a stub has no user-visible benefit
yet. scripts/build-dtb.sh applies the equivalent change with fdtput straight
to the shipped DTB, which avoids a kernel rebuild.

Apply against AsahiLinux/linux, branch `asahi`.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112.dtsi
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 
 	aliases {
 		gpu = &gpu;
+		sep = &sep;
 		#ifdef APPLE_USE_PMP
 		pmp = &pmp;
 		#endif
@@ -1649,7 +1650,7 @@
 			mboxes = <&sep_mbox>;
 			mbox-names = "mbox";
 			iommus = <&sep_dart 0>;
-			status = "disabled";
+			status = "okay";
 		};
 
 		sep_mbox: mbox@25e408000 {
